# View models

Shapes the screen shows live in `src/view-models`. Other layers import them only through `@/view-models`.

- One view model per file. The file name matches the type: `NamedItemVm` becomes `named-item-vm.ts`.
- The type name ends with `Vm`.
- A view model is not changed after it is created. Every field is `readonly`, and lists are `readonly T[]`.
- The type and every field have a short English comment: what it shows, and when the value is empty. Leave a blank line between fields. The comment stays immediately above its field.
- A view model may use types from `@/models`. It does not import `services`, `dtos`, `queries`, `feature`, `widgets`, `pages`, `app`, or `ui`.

```typescript
// Bad: the same shape declared again inside a feature
export type NamedItem = { id: number; name: string; image: string };

// Good
/** An item with its catalog name and image. */
export type NamedItemVm = {
  /** Item id in the Dota catalog. */
  readonly id: number;

  /** Display name. */
  readonly name: string;

  /** Image URL. Empty when the catalog has no image. */
  readonly image: string;
};
```
